  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f7d4b697-04df-53ff-8212-d5967b410e21" activityNameId="24d034d2-8633-56f2-aec3-9fbe17592e87" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cotton fibres, ginned, at farm</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cotton fibres, ginned, at farm
The multioutput-process "cotton production" delivers the co-products "cotton fibres, ginned, at farm", "cotton seed, at farm". The allocation is based on economic criteria and on mass balance. World production of ginned cotton was 26.2 Mt in 2005. The inventory refers to 1 kg dry fibres and 1.77 kg seed from standard China production.;
UUID: 4e1dc5c9-832f-3030-8410-143fd7488787
The inventories include the cultivation of cotton upon Chinese standards. Included steps are soil cultivation, pestizides fertilisation (mineral fertilizer), harvest, loading for transport and extraction of the fibres in a gin plant
Location: Data mainly from expert gremiums of respective country
Technology: Cultivation of cotton upon Chinese conventional production standards
Time period: undefined
Production volume: World production of cotton fibres was 26.2 Mt in 2005.
Sampling: Literature data. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4e1dc5c9-832f-3030-8410-143fd7488787.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
